            "embedding_text": "Authority: Social_Engineering\n\n        Document: 1-s2.0-S016686-main\n\n        Chapter:\n        \n        \n\n        Section:\n        \n\n        Heading:\n        \n\n        Content:\n\n        Phishing susceptibility is influenced by a combination of cognitive, behavioral, and contextual factors, including perceived cyber-risk, self-efficacy in detecting phishing emails, routine internet activities, and device usage. Contradictions with prior research—such as the lack of a significant link between prior victimization and susceptibility—highlight the need for nuanced understanding of fraud indicators and behavioral patterns."
